IED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905833957","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905833957","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-12-20","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219","date":"2024-12-19","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":4,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905935951","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905935951","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-12-19","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219","date":"2024-12-19","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-04","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: Based on information provided during a DFPS investigation it was determined that did not demonstrate competency of caring for the children and meeting their needs in a timely manner, as one child was observed visibly upset during the time and was not comforted by any of the caregivers present.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026658327","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1203-3-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219","date":"2024-12-19","original_code":"746.1203(3)(D)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-04","finding":"Personal use of electronic devices, such as cell phones, MP3 players, tablets, and video games: Based on information provided during a DFPS investigation it was determined that the previous center director had notified the caregivers of the concerns of using their cell phones while supervising the children, but no policy had been put in place. The caregivers were both observed using their phones during the times of the incidents.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026655045","violation_type_title":"Personal use of electronic devices, such as cell phones, MP3 players, tablets, and video games (26 TAC §746.1203(3)(D))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219","date":"2024-12-19","original_code":"746.1201(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-04","finding":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited: Based on information provided during a DFPS investigation it was determined that two caregivers handled a child in an aggressive manner physically. These actions resulted in Reason to Believe listings for both caregivers.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026652491","violation_type_title":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited (26 TAC §746.1201(4))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2805","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241219","date":"2024-12-19","original_code":"746.2805","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-03-04","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - No Harsh, Cruel or Unusual: Based on information provided during a DFPS investigation it was determined that caregivers were observed mishandling children in care during naptime by pushing their heads into their nap mat, hitting the children on their heads, and aggressively straighten their legs out to make them lay down while in care.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026655047","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - No Harsh, Cruel or Unusual (26 TAC §746.2805)","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241218","date":"2024-12-18","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":3,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905935950","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905935950","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-12-18","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241218-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1613-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241218","date":"2024-12-18","original_code":"746.1613(a)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-01-30","finding":"Reduction of child/caregiver naptime ratio by 50% allowed, If 13 or more children in care, children are 18 mo. or older and other standards met: This standard was tasked over for this investigation and found to be deficient. During this investigation and video footage review, it was determined that there was a total of 12 children, ages 12-17 months, with only one caregiver present during naptime. This is not allowed for this age group of children, as the caregiver/child ratio cannot be reduced for the group.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026633458","violation_type_title":"Reduction of child/caregiver naptime ratio by 50% allowed, If 13 or more children in care, children are 18 mo. or older and other standards met (26 TAC §746.1613(a))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241218-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2805-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241218","date":"2024-12-18","original_code":"746.2805(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-01-30","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - Corporal Punishment: This standard was tasked over for this investigation and found to be deficient. A caregiver was observed mishandling a child in care during naptime by pushing the child's head into their nap mat and aggressively straighten their legs out to make them lay down while in care.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026633461","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - Corporal Punishment (26 TAC §746.2805(1))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241218-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241218","date":"2024-12-18","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-01-30","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: This standard was tasked over for this investigation and found to be deficient. During this investigation it was determined that the caregiver left in charge of the children during naptime did not practice self-control when she mishandled the children during this time.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026633460","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1335166-i20241212","date":"2024-12-12","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905935949","url":"htt